6588","position":"1786674468698792863-87c21523-915d-42f0-9501-857c72bcbd4b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"rebar-debug RCA and pre-Gerrit repair report.\n\nProblem: the bridge cadence proof consumed 100.66-130.59s in every Ubuntu matrix cell, despite asserting one immutable workflow schedule.\n\nProven root cause: tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py called _bridge_schedule() inside the 24*60 minute scan. Each call reparsed reconcile-bridge.yml, so one invariant was loaded 1,440 times. Runtime counting observed the repeated boundary executing; hoisting only that acquisition collapsed the same exhaustive proof from a 8.75s local median (14.12/8.30/8.75s) to 0.59s (0.60/0.59/0.57s), rejecting cron matching itself as the dominant cost. The explicit CI performance requirement and test contract classify this as a defect. No caller behavior depends on repeated parsing.\n\nRED/GREEN: a focused boundary-count oracle in test_bridge_backstop_fires_on_a_uniform_hourly_cadence failed before the repair because parses exceeded one. It was physically held out from the fixer. The fixer hoisted schedule = _bridge_schedule() above the comprehension while retaining all 1,440 minute evaluations, the exact 24 fires, and the circular 60-minute gap proof. The held-out oracle then passed. Reintroducing _bridge_schedule() inside the loop returned it to RED; restoring the hoist returned it to GREEN. The observable assertion is boundary invocation count plus unchanged cadence results, so behavior-preserving refactors remain green.\n\nReplication and safety: focused file 37 passed; make lint and make typecheck passed from the worktree venv; pre-commit repeated lint/typecheck successfully. Same-host wall time fell 8.16s / 93.3% locally without reducing assertions, platform cells, or coverage. No production code, dependency, external effect, or test weakening is involved. Construct sweep found no other repeated _bridge_schedule call in this proof; no parity surfaces apply to a test-local helper. Residual risk: the separate test-wide YAML/AST/Pandoc repeated-boundary patterns remain tracked on linked remediation tickets, not hidden in this fix. Commit 4c4225c3dd is ready for Gerrit once the existing unrelated CI run completes.","timestamp":1786673254867079001}],"created_at":1786671641985083001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"a5c7b431-f547-4b11-9ecd-adc26720de81","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4f50-b1f2-78af-4326"},{"link_uuid":"87c21523-915d-42f0-9501-857c72bcbd4b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"94ef-c770-1662-4e23"}],"description":"## Context\nGerrit Verified run 31752047186 spent 100.66-130.59s per Ubuntu cell in `test_bridge_backstop_fires_on_a_uniform_hourly_cadence`. Runtime tracing proves `_bridge_schedule()` reparses the same workflow YAML inside the 1,440-minute comprehension. Local current=7.925s, invariant reuse=0.00106s. The exhaustive cadence proof is valuable; repeated YAML parsing is not. This remediation matches invariant-sharing practice in pytest, Django, and Pylint/Astroid. No prior rejection was found; `coercive-paediatric-bug` rejects added parallelism without aggregate savings, which this does not use.\n\n## Plan\n- Strengthen the existing unit test with a behavioral oracle that counts schedule acquisition and requires one acquisition per cadence proof while preserving all 1,440 minute evaluations and exact gap assertion.\n- Hoist the immutable schedule value once before the comprehension.\n- Run the held-out RED→GREEN and defect-seeded mutation check, the focused policy suite, lint/typecheck, and paired timing runs.\n- Land through Gerrit and record observed Ubuntu runner-time savings; back-out is a Gerrit revert restoring the prior comprehension.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The cadence test still evaluates every one of the 1,440 minutes and asserts uniform 60-minute circular gaps.\n- [ ] A unit oracle proves workflow schedule acquisition occurs once, fails on the current 1,440-read implementation, and passes after the change.\n- [ ] Reintroducing schedule acquisition inside the minute loop returns the oracle to RED.\n- [ ] Paired local timing demonstrates the repeated YAML parsing cost is eliminated without new jobs or reduced coverage.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, typecheck, Gerrit LLM-Review +1, and Gerrit Verified +1 pass before merge.\n- [ ] The final ticket comment records RED/GREEN/mutation evidence and measured savings.","env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_tickets_push_policy.py","reason":"Hoist immutable workflow schedule acquisition and add the focused behavioral regression oracle."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","managed_refs":[["relates_to","94ef-c770-1662-4e23"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"9e4dd634-db1e-4aaf-85fb-f9932e4bb2a6","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["ci","performance","ubuntu","test"],"ticket_id":"f936-a0b9-e5f8-4def","ticket_type":"task","title":"Hoist bridge schedule parsing out of minute scan","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7d780012-a586-40d2-a236-cc932a5f9a7a","2ae8e61c-e6b7-49ce-880c-c16b4e66e7d7","a5c7b431-f547-4b11-9ecd-adc26720de81","57c0373f-dcd0-474e-840c-52c2ea3f2abd","9e4dd634-db1e-4aaf-85fb-f9932e4bb2a6","533eeea0-6307-4f4c-a682-85351b164051","60cdc307-b113-48